    "## 13. Key Takeaways and Best Practices"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Best Practices for Hierarchical Forecasting\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Start Simple**: Begin with statistical models (ARIMA, ETS) as baselines\n",
    "2. **Feature Engineering**: Lag features, rolling statistics, and temporal features are crucial\n",
    "3. **Hierarchical Structure**: Define clear hierarchy levels before modeling\n",
    "4. **Reconciliation**: Always apply hierarchical reconciliation to ensure consistency\n",
    "5. **Uncertainty Quantification**: Use conformal prediction or probabilistic models\n",
    "6. **Ensemble Methods**: Combining multiple models often outperforms single models\n",
    "7. **Validation**: Use rolling window validation for time series\n",
    "\n",
    "### When to Use Each Model\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Best For | Data Requirements |\n",
    "|-------|----------|-------------------|\n",
    "| Gradient Boosting | Tabular features, interpretable | Medium (1-2 years) |\n",
    "| LSTM | Long-term dependencies | Long (2+ years) |\n",
    "| DeepAR | Probabilistic forecasts | Medium-Long |\n",
    "| N-BEATS | Univariate, interpretable | Medium |\n",
    "| TFT | Multi-variate, covariates | Long (2+ years) |\n",
    "| Ensemble | Production robustness | Any |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Next Steps for Production\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Implement with GluonTS/NeuralForecast** for SOTA models\n",
    "2. **Add external covariates**: Weather, promotions, economic indicators\n",
    "3. **Automated retraining**: Schedule daily/weekly model updates\n",
    "4. **Monitoring**: Track forecast accuracy over time\n",
    "5. **A/B testing**: Compare model versions in production\n",
    "6. **Edge deployment**: Use ONNX/TensorRT for real-time inference"
   ]
